1
00:00:56,797 --> 00:00:58,256
Can you still drive?

2
00:00:58,256 --> 00:01:00,175
Do you want to stay at our condo for a bit?

3
00:01:05,734 --> 00:01:06,276
Ke!

4
00:01:06,276 --> 00:01:07,140
Hi, Luna.

5
00:01:07,944 --> 00:01:09,112
Don’t you “Hi, Luna” me.

6
00:01:10,822 --> 00:01:12,032
How’d you get this shirt?

7
00:01:12,324 --> 00:01:13,533
From her ex, Kalix.

8
00:01:14,326 --> 00:01:15,827
I can cook. Is that okay?

9
00:01:15,827 --> 00:01:18,622
Huh? You’re not allowed
to use our kitchen.

10
00:01:18,788 --> 00:01:20,624
Can you two please stop fighting?

11
00:01:22,667 --> 00:01:23,574
For you.

12
00:01:24,711 --> 00:01:26,212
You’re together now.

13
00:01:27,297 --> 00:01:28,798
Didn’t she kiss you before?

14
00:01:29,049 --> 00:01:30,091
I’m with her cousin.

15
00:01:32,218 --> 00:01:33,470
You mean, Kierra?

16
00:01:36,139 --> 00:01:39,100
You know, Luna, he says he still loves you.

17
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:40,477
As if.

18
00:01:40,477 --> 00:01:41,728
He loves me?

19
00:01:43,313 --> 00:01:44,856
No, no, I’m fine now.

20
00:01:45,982 --> 00:01:47,567
Welcome to our Bataan house!

21
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:49,069
This is for your mom.

22
00:01:49,069 --> 00:01:50,403
Let me introduce you.

23
00:01:50,487 --> 00:01:53,657
Mommy! My friend’s here.

24
00:01:53,698 --> 00:01:54,741
This is for you.

25
00:01:59,079 --> 00:02:00,997
You’re such a great father, Uncle.

26
00:02:01,414 --> 00:02:04,417
It’s no surprise to me that Kierra is
the way she is. It’s because of you, too.

27
00:02:04,793 --> 00:02:08,296
I heard my name. Are you
talking about me, Daddy?

28
00:02:08,797 --> 00:02:11,508
Don’t tell him too many
things about me, okay?

29
00:02:13,218 --> 00:02:15,303
Your bangs are getting kind of long.

30
00:02:15,303 --> 00:02:16,429
Yeah, they are.

31
00:02:17,597 --> 00:02:18,431
It’s pretty.

32
00:02:21,768 --> 00:02:22,644
Thank you.

33
00:03:50,565 --> 00:03:52,817
I’m sure your cooking is more appetizing.

34
00:03:52,817 --> 00:03:54,819
It’s Christmas so it should taste good.

35
00:03:55,528 --> 00:03:56,905
Mommy, Daddy!

36
00:03:56,988 --> 00:03:57,447
Oh!

37
00:03:58,031 --> 00:03:59,240
- Hi, Uncle.
- Shan.

38
00:03:59,324 --> 00:04:00,700
Uncle, Auntie, good evening.

39
00:04:01,826 --> 00:04:03,328
- Hello!
- Good evening.

40
00:04:03,828 --> 00:04:05,580
This is who I was talking about.

41
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,625
Uncle Abel and Auntie Sonia.

42
00:04:08,708 --> 00:04:10,794
And my cousin, Rona.

43
00:04:10,835 --> 00:04:13,004
Her siblings, Tofel and Tintin.

44
00:04:13,004 --> 00:04:13,671
Tin.

45
00:04:13,797 --> 00:04:16,716
Nice meeting you, Ke’s boyfriend.

46
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:17,675
He’s a friend, Uncle.

47
00:04:17,675 --> 00:04:18,343
Just a friend.

48
00:04:18,718 --> 00:04:20,887
Such a celebrity response, Kierra.

49
00:04:21,429 --> 00:04:24,641
Oh, stop it. He might feel awkward.

50
00:04:25,475 --> 00:04:29,395
Yeah, stop it. She
said they’re just friends.

51
00:04:29,395 --> 00:04:30,647
- Friends.
- Yes.

52
00:04:30,647 --> 00:04:32,816
But they’re actually soulmates.

53
00:04:32,941 --> 00:04:35,152
How did we become soulmates, Mommy?

54
00:04:35,777 --> 00:04:38,321
Don’t you remember
when you two were little?

55
00:04:38,346 --> 00:04:41,182
Didn’t you always chase after him?
You were always following him around.

56
00:04:41,282 --> 00:04:43,743
That’s why he was annoyed with you,
because you were so persistent.

57
00:04:44,118 --> 00:04:45,078
Really, Auntie?

58
00:04:46,162 --> 00:04:47,580
- Yes.
- It’s not true.

59
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:48,873
I never did any of that.

60
00:04:49,249 --> 00:04:50,416
Are you sure?

61
00:04:50,416 --> 00:04:51,876
You really weren’t
following him around then?

62
00:04:51,901 --> 00:04:53,778
I see you’ve had a crush
on me since we were kids.

63
00:04:53,806 --> 00:04:55,516
Stop it, you guys.

64
00:04:55,672 --> 00:04:58,258
And you, don’t ride with their jokes.

65
00:04:58,424 --> 00:04:59,175
Oh my.

66
00:04:59,175 --> 00:05:00,385
Come on, let’s take some pictures.

67
00:05:00,385 --> 00:05:02,220
- Oh, yes, sure. Good idea!
- Yeah, let’s do it.

68
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:03,638
- So we can pass the time while we wait.
- Let them go first.

69
00:05:03,638 --> 00:05:04,973
- You two first.
- Yes. Sure, you two go first.

70
00:05:04,973 --> 00:05:05,974
Here, over here.

71
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:07,725
- There.
- There you go.

72
00:05:09,519 --> 00:05:10,478
Okay, ready—

73
00:05:10,895 --> 00:05:14,065
Shan, are you Ayi’s boyfriend?

74
00:05:15,538 --> 00:05:16,956
No, we’re just friends.

75
00:05:17,289 --> 00:05:19,148
No way, looks like you’re
her boyfriend, though.

76
00:05:19,821 --> 00:05:21,072
We’re just friends.

77
00:05:21,364 --> 00:05:26,160
I wish you were her boyfriend so
you could always be with us here.

78
00:05:28,079 --> 00:05:28,997
I hope so, too.

79
00:05:30,415 --> 00:05:31,875
Come on, them and the kids.

80
00:05:31,875 --> 00:05:33,668
- Yes, the whole family.
- Go take your photos with them.

81
00:05:33,668 --> 00:05:34,544
The whole family now.

82
00:05:34,544 --> 00:05:35,461
Okay, the whole family.

83
00:05:36,254 --> 00:05:37,714
Make sure it’s nice.

84
00:05:37,797 --> 00:05:38,423
Okay.

85
00:05:38,631 --> 00:05:39,299
Ready now.

86
00:05:39,299 --> 00:05:39,591
Smile!

87
00:05:39,591 --> 00:05:43,887
- One, two, three, go!
- Wacky shots next!

88
00:05:45,013 --> 00:05:46,681
- Everyone together.
- Everyone now?

89
00:05:46,681 --> 00:05:47,724
All of us, the family.

90
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:49,350
Let’s take a family photo.

91
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:50,351
- All of us?
- Okay.

92
00:05:50,351 --> 00:05:51,644
- Let me do it.
- Shan, do you mind?

93
00:05:51,669 --> 00:05:52,419
- I’ll do it.
- Yeah.

94
00:05:53,229 --> 00:05:54,939
We need to take a photo of us 3, too.

95
00:05:55,023 --> 00:05:56,274
Hurry, Shan will take the photo.

96
00:05:56,274 --> 00:05:57,199
Come on.

97
00:05:57,233 --> 00:05:58,109
Closer please.

98
00:05:58,109 --> 00:06:01,154
One, two, three—

99
00:06:01,266 --> 00:06:03,226
- Now, everyone. Wacky shots.
- Wacky poses!

100
00:06:04,032 --> 00:06:06,284
One, two, three.

101
00:06:06,659 --> 00:06:08,244
Now that girl who has
a crush on me, smile now.

102
00:06:08,244 --> 00:06:10,788
- Wow!
- One, two, three—

103
00:06:12,457 --> 00:06:14,201
Seems like he’s just
taking a photo of you!

104
00:06:14,225 --> 00:06:14,792
Okay.

105
00:06:14,792 --> 00:06:15,460
Let me take a photo of both of you.

106
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:16,502
No, we’re good.

107
00:06:16,502 --> 00:06:17,795
Come on, both of you.

108
00:06:17,795 --> 00:06:19,255
Come on, hurry.

109
00:06:19,255 --> 00:06:20,298
The one who has a crush—

110
00:06:20,298 --> 00:06:21,424
- So you two will—
- Mommy!

111
00:06:21,424 --> 00:06:22,842
- The one who has a crush on Ke.
- What crush?

112
00:06:22,842 --> 00:06:24,177
Don’t get it to your head.
You’re going too far.

113
00:06:24,177 --> 00:06:25,053
You’re getting a little too giddy.
You’re way too happy.

114
00:06:25,053 --> 00:06:27,221
This way we have a remembrance,
because Ke always forgets.

115
00:06:27,221 --> 00:06:27,722
Yeah.

116
00:06:27,722 --> 00:06:30,600
- One, two—
- Smile!

117
00:06:31,559 --> 00:06:32,727
So sweet.

118
00:06:33,603 --> 00:06:35,063
- You have a crush on me, huh?
- Move a little closer.

119
00:06:35,563 --> 00:06:36,731
Ready. One, two, three—

120
00:06:36,731 --> 00:06:38,316
They’re feeling awkward, Dad.

121
00:06:38,524 --> 00:06:39,233
Look, it’s nice.

122
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:40,485
Hey, let’s go inside first.

123
00:06:40,902 --> 00:06:41,778
They left us.

124
00:06:41,778 --> 00:06:43,154
Come on, I’m hungry.

125
00:06:43,154 --> 00:06:43,947
We’ll leave you guys here, okay?

126
00:06:43,947 --> 00:06:44,906
- Okay.
- Sure!

127
00:06:47,909 --> 00:06:49,744
Sorry for my family. Too much?

128
00:06:49,744 --> 00:06:51,996
No, it’s okay. It’s fine, it’s fine.

129
00:06:52,997 --> 00:06:54,040
I like your family.

130
00:06:55,124 --> 00:06:55,917
It’s all fun.

131
00:06:56,751 --> 00:06:57,669
Your family’s nice.

132
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:01,381
Want a solo photo?
I’ll take a picture of you.

133
00:07:01,714 --> 00:07:02,590
No, it’s okay.

134
00:07:02,715 --> 00:07:03,716
I’m not photogenic.

135
00:07:04,092 --> 00:07:06,344
I look ugly in pictures.
I don’t like my face.

136
00:07:06,594 --> 00:07:07,428
No way.

137
00:07:07,971 --> 00:07:09,389
I’ve always admired how you look.

138
00:07:09,973 --> 00:07:11,599
In photos or in person.

139
00:07:11,766 --> 00:07:14,978
Actually, you look
better in person. Much better.

140
00:07:16,229 --> 00:07:17,563
Come on, let me take your picture.

141
00:07:18,648 --> 00:07:19,315
Okay.

142
00:07:19,315 --> 00:07:19,857
Let’s go.

143
00:07:21,901 --> 00:07:22,443
Here?

144
00:07:22,468 --> 00:07:23,511
Yeah, stand here.

145
00:07:23,861 --> 00:07:26,538
Right there. Yeah, that way
you’ve got a nice background.

146
00:07:27,843 --> 00:07:29,553
One, two, three—
Smile, come on.

147
00:07:29,578 --> 00:07:30,495
One, two, three—

148
00:07:31,545 --> 00:07:32,495
One more.

149
00:07:32,495 --> 00:07:33,955
One, two...

150
00:07:34,789 --> 00:07:36,082
Look at her, she’s got a crush on me.

151
00:07:36,082 --> 00:07:37,667
One, two, three—

152
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,086
Look, you look great.

153
00:07:44,716 --> 00:07:46,718
- Thank you.
- See? Pretty.

154
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:49,053
Post this, okay? I’ll wait for it.

155
00:08:01,649 --> 00:08:02,275
Cheers!

156
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,985
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

157
00:08:04,027 --> 00:08:07,697
- Merry Christmas!
- Merry Christmas!

158
00:08:07,697 --> 00:08:08,823
Merry Christmas, Dad!

159
00:08:08,823 --> 00:08:10,616
Merry Christmas.

160
00:08:11,242 --> 00:08:12,285
Let’s eat, come on.

161
00:08:12,285 --> 00:08:12,994
- Grab some over there.
- Come on, hurry.

162
00:08:15,621 --> 00:08:16,539
Merry Christmas.

163
00:08:17,498 --> 00:08:18,708
Merry Christmas.

164
00:08:19,459 --> 00:08:20,835
Thank you for bringing me here.

165
00:08:20,835 --> 00:08:23,004
I told you you’d
have a good time here.

166
00:08:23,546 --> 00:08:25,048
And I’m glad you’re happy.

167
00:08:26,924 --> 00:08:27,967
I am, too.

168
00:08:31,054 --> 00:08:31,846
What’s wrong?

169
00:08:33,973 --> 00:08:35,516
An arrow hit my heart.

170
00:08:38,227 --> 00:08:41,481
Another hit! I’m gonna fall in this state.
Another hit! I’ve been hit too much.

171
00:08:55,661 --> 00:08:57,246
You want some?

172
00:09:38,405 --> 00:09:42,325
- Merry Christmas!
- Oh! Thank you. Wow.

173
00:09:42,867 --> 00:09:43,910
This one’s also for you.

174
00:09:44,377 --> 00:09:46,170
Wow.

175
00:09:46,295 --> 00:09:47,547
This is a lot.

176
00:09:48,673 --> 00:09:49,465
Here.

177
00:09:50,414 --> 00:09:51,582
Christmas Special.

178
00:09:51,926 --> 00:09:53,261
I made all of these.

179
00:09:53,386 --> 00:09:56,389
Wow! Thank you!

180
00:09:57,890 --> 00:10:00,101
- You sure this is good?
- That’s delicious.

181
00:10:00,101 --> 00:10:01,519
Oh, so you really made these.

182
00:10:02,019 --> 00:10:04,313
Oh no, I didn’t get you anything.

183
00:10:04,879 --> 00:10:07,882
Come on, it’s fine. Do you
know what gift you gave me?

184
00:10:08,635 --> 00:10:09,970
You brought me here.

185
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,530
Oh. Wait, I actually have one.

186
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:13,531
Wait.

187
00:10:17,853 --> 00:10:20,816
Dad bought this because
we’re taking a family picture later.

188
00:10:20,841 --> 00:10:21,883
So just put it on.

189
00:10:22,748 --> 00:10:25,293
Huh? I’m not part of your family.

190
00:10:25,293 --> 00:10:26,878
I’ll just take the picture.

191
00:10:27,837 --> 00:10:30,089
Well, you’re a part
of my life now, right?

192
00:10:30,214 --> 00:10:31,549
So go on, wear it.

193
00:10:36,137 --> 00:10:37,180
I hope it fits.

194
00:10:37,221 --> 00:10:38,055
It’ll fit.

195
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:45,563
How does it look?

196
00:10:46,022 --> 00:10:47,815
Nice. It fits.

197
00:10:49,317 --> 00:10:50,693
To be part of your life.

198
00:10:51,569 --> 00:10:52,570
Come on.

199
00:10:52,778 --> 00:10:54,030
Let’s put this here.

200
00:10:54,697 --> 00:10:56,157
So they can try it.

201
00:10:56,574 --> 00:10:59,076
Wow, you’re already wearing the sweater.

202
00:10:59,076 --> 00:11:00,119
How nice!

203
00:11:00,144 --> 00:11:00,936
Thank you.

204
00:11:00,995 --> 00:11:01,954
Should we put this here, Mom?

205
00:11:01,954 --> 00:11:03,456
Yes, just here, Dad.

206
00:11:04,415 --> 00:11:06,626
Perfect timing since you’re
already in your sweater,

207
00:11:06,626 --> 00:11:09,503
Let’s take a Christmas
picture before breakfast.

208
00:11:09,503 --> 00:11:10,421
- Yeah.
- Right?

209
00:11:10,463 --> 00:11:11,088
That’s right.

210
00:11:11,088 --> 00:11:11,464
Okay.

211
00:11:11,464 --> 00:11:12,465
I’ll fix the tripod.

212
00:11:12,465 --> 00:11:13,925
- Hold on.
- Yes, please.

213
00:11:15,718 --> 00:11:17,678
Ah, I’ll get it.

214
00:11:22,558 --> 00:11:24,769
Oh, Theo! You’re here.

215
00:11:24,769 --> 00:11:25,770
Come in.

216
00:11:25,978 --> 00:11:27,897
Yeah, we were already in Subic,

217
00:11:27,897 --> 00:11:31,984
so when you invited me to Bataan,
I figured I’d drop by to say hi.

218
00:11:32,902 --> 00:11:33,986
And, I brought a gift.

219
00:11:34,237 --> 00:11:36,030
Perfect timing, since we’re
about to have breakfast.

220
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:37,323
No. It’s fine.

221
00:11:37,323 --> 00:11:38,407
I wouldn’t want to impose.

222
00:11:40,243 --> 00:11:41,661
- Looks good on you.
- Thank you.

223
00:11:41,661 --> 00:11:42,620
Of course.

224
00:11:43,204 --> 00:11:43,871
Oh. I’ll  just check on her.

225
00:11:43,871 --> 00:11:44,538
Sure.

226
00:11:44,747 --> 00:11:46,791
Don’t be shy. Mommy already knows you.

227
00:11:46,791 --> 00:11:49,877
You know how she is. It’s embarrassing.

228
00:11:49,877 --> 00:11:51,254
- Come on, don’t be shy.
- Ke.

229
00:11:53,881 --> 00:11:55,216
You’re—

230
00:11:55,967 --> 00:11:57,426
You’re the—

231
00:11:58,719 --> 00:12:00,388
You’re the barista
from the coffee shop.

232
00:12:01,597 --> 00:12:03,933
And you’re the one who
spilled coffee at the coffee shop.

233
00:12:15,903 --> 00:12:17,780
Shan, this is Theo.

234
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:19,407
Theo, this is Shan.

235
00:12:20,332 --> 00:12:22,751
Yeah. I remember him.

236
00:12:23,846 --> 00:12:25,597
Don’t you go to the
cafe with him sometimes?

237
00:12:25,871 --> 00:12:26,910
Right.

238
00:12:29,292 --> 00:12:30,376
So it is you.

239
00:12:35,462 --> 00:12:36,755
Your coffee there is so good.

240
00:12:37,508 --> 00:12:38,356
Thank you.

241
00:12:39,074 --> 00:12:40,743
Come back anytime, my treat.

242
00:12:54,984 --> 00:12:55,818
Let’s go.

243
00:12:56,235 --> 00:12:57,653
Come on, let’s go.

244
00:12:58,274 --> 00:13:01,193
We’re having breakfast,
so don’t be shy, come on.

245
00:13:01,407 --> 00:13:03,075
- There.
- This is the center.

246
00:13:03,406 --> 00:13:04,366
Here.

247
00:13:05,202 --> 00:13:06,162
There.

248
00:13:07,371 --> 00:13:08,331
Mommy, Daddy.

249
00:13:08,456 --> 00:13:08,956
Yes?

250
00:13:08,956 --> 00:13:10,958
This is Theo. You’ve met him before, right?

251
00:13:10,958 --> 00:13:12,543
He’s our friend from school.

252
00:13:12,543 --> 00:13:13,377
Yes, yes.

253
00:13:13,586 --> 00:13:16,047
- Hello, Merry Christmas!
- Merry Christmas.

254
00:13:16,096 --> 00:13:17,806
Actually, I got you guys a gift.

255
00:13:18,132 --> 00:13:19,133
- Wow
- Oh, wow.

256
00:13:19,133 --> 00:13:21,010
- Thank you! Thank you.
- Wow.

257
00:13:21,010 --> 00:13:23,220
- You’re so nice, thank you.
- You know what, Theo—

258
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:24,013
Join us.

259
00:13:24,305 --> 00:13:25,097
We’re taking a picture.

260
00:13:25,097 --> 00:13:26,390
- It’s fine, really.
- Oh, yes. Come on.

261
00:13:26,390 --> 00:13:28,434
- Come on, join us.
- Come on.

262
00:13:28,476 --> 00:13:29,769
- I’m not even wearing a sweater.
- Hurry.

263
00:13:29,769 --> 00:13:30,644
- It’s okay.
- That’s fine.

264
00:13:30,644 --> 00:13:31,562
Come on, come on, it’s okay.

265
00:13:31,645 --> 00:13:32,897
- Is it connected?
- Yes.

266
00:13:32,897 --> 00:13:33,731
- There you go.
- I’ll just stand on this side, then.

267
00:13:33,731 --> 00:13:34,273
Yes.

268
00:13:34,357 --> 00:13:35,274
There, perfect.

269
00:13:35,399 --> 00:13:37,109
There you go. Merry Christmas.

270
00:13:37,193 --> 00:13:38,402
Okay. Okay, guys. Ready.

271
00:13:38,402 --> 00:13:39,111
Ready.

272
00:13:39,737 --> 00:13:40,905
Let me hide it.

273
00:13:41,322 --> 00:13:42,073
Smile.

274
00:13:42,073 --> 00:13:43,115
Smile!

275
00:13:43,532 --> 00:13:43,866
One more.

276
00:13:43,866 --> 00:13:44,617
One more?

277
00:13:50,630 --> 00:13:51,923
- There.
- Okay.

278
00:13:52,674 --> 00:13:53,876
- Let’s see.
- Let me see.

279
00:13:53,876 --> 00:13:54,877
That’s nice!

280
00:13:54,877 --> 00:13:56,670
- Nice!
- So nice!

281
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:57,922
This looks good.

282
00:13:58,172 --> 00:13:59,131
It looks good.

283
00:13:59,131 --> 00:14:00,633
- One more, wacky poses now.
- Nice!

284
00:14:00,633 --> 00:14:02,635
- One more wacky pose.
- Wacky, okay?

285
00:14:03,302 --> 00:14:05,429
One, two, three.

286
00:14:08,391 --> 00:14:09,433
Hope that’s good.

287
00:14:09,767 --> 00:14:11,185
There you go.

288
00:14:11,185 --> 00:14:12,311
- Why do I look so stupid?
- Nice.

289
00:14:12,311 --> 00:14:15,523
I don’t know. It’s supposed
to be a wacky pose.

290
00:14:15,606 --> 00:14:17,024
Come on, let’s eat already.

291
00:14:17,108 --> 00:14:18,567
Come on, let’s go.

292
00:14:18,692 --> 00:14:20,861
- Come on, let’s eat.
- Let’s eat.

293
00:14:20,986 --> 00:14:23,114
Serve that, too. It looks delicious.

294
00:14:23,114 --> 00:14:24,073
There.

295
00:14:24,073 --> 00:14:24,657
Okay, sit down.

296
00:14:24,657 --> 00:14:27,451
- Do you like this kind of food, Theo?
- Yes.

297
00:14:29,195 --> 00:14:30,738
Thanks again for inviting me.

298
00:14:30,763 --> 00:14:33,433
Of course, you’re close by anyway.

299
00:14:34,208 --> 00:14:35,000
Thank you.

300
00:14:35,626 --> 00:14:39,046
Sure, I’ll let you know.

301
00:14:45,790 --> 00:14:49,710
You look so happy. It’s so obvious.

302
00:14:51,522 --> 00:14:52,732
Okay.

303
00:14:56,105 --> 00:14:57,815
I can’t remember anyway.

304
00:15:01,485 --> 00:15:02,945
It’s alright.

305
00:15:07,805 --> 00:15:08,555
Yup.

306
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:15,332
So…

307
00:15:17,376 --> 00:15:18,544
You like him, don’t you?

308
00:15:19,879 --> 00:15:21,672
Who? Shan?

309
00:15:26,177 --> 00:15:28,179
Yes. I like him.

310
00:15:28,888 --> 00:15:33,309
But we’re taking it slow, because you
know what happened in my last relationship.

311
00:15:38,189 --> 00:15:39,648
Yeah, that’s good.

312
00:15:40,858 --> 00:15:42,401
That’s probably better, too.

313
00:15:43,194 --> 00:15:47,114
What matters is that you’re happy again.

314
00:15:49,074 --> 00:15:51,952
So I’m happy for you.

315
00:15:53,902 --> 00:15:54,903
Really, really happy.

316
00:15:56,957 --> 00:15:58,334
Why so serious?

317
00:16:03,144 --> 00:16:06,105
Looks like I’ve missed my chance.

318
00:16:07,343 --> 00:16:08,928
Your chance at what?

319
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:18,771
To make you happy too, I guess.

320
00:16:23,535 --> 00:16:25,746
Oh, whatever! You’re always joking around.

321
00:16:26,195 --> 00:16:32,326
Of course I’m happy, because
of my family and my friends.

322
00:16:36,288 --> 00:16:38,374
I just wonder sometimes,

323
00:16:41,752 --> 00:16:43,295
what if it were me?

324
00:16:46,715 --> 00:16:47,716
What do you mean?

325
00:16:48,884 --> 00:16:50,678
You keep cutting yourself off. Tell me—

326
00:16:50,678 --> 00:16:52,388
- What do you mean?
- Nothing.

327
00:16:52,821 --> 00:16:54,990
Nothing. Don’t mind it. It’s just that—

328
00:16:56,183 --> 00:17:01,313
we’ve been friends for so long,
and it feels good to see you happy.

329
00:17:01,939 --> 00:17:05,150
As long as you’re okay, I’m okay too.

330
00:17:06,026 --> 00:17:06,986
All right?

331
00:17:07,663 --> 00:17:10,290
Come on, let’s go. Your parents
are probably looking for us.

332
00:17:10,315 --> 00:17:11,150
And—

333
00:17:11,644 --> 00:17:13,437
Shan might get jealous.

334
00:17:14,014 --> 00:17:15,808
Why would he be jealous?

335
00:17:16,120 --> 00:17:17,663
He’s not like that. Don’t be silly.

336
00:17:21,125 --> 00:17:21,875
Ke.

337
00:17:22,626 --> 00:17:24,336
Come help me with the gifts.

338
00:17:25,170 --> 00:17:26,171
Okay, Mommy.

339
00:17:26,171 --> 00:17:27,006
Let’s go.

340
00:17:27,673 --> 00:17:28,966
I’ll get to that later.

341
00:17:35,139 --> 00:17:36,640
See you, bro. Take care.

342
00:17:37,099 --> 00:17:38,684
Yeah, see you.

343
00:17:39,226 --> 00:17:42,730
Oh, and tell Auntie and Uncle
that I had a great time.

344
00:17:43,147 --> 00:17:43,897
Okay.

345
00:17:44,565 --> 00:17:45,232
Take care!

346
00:17:45,232 --> 00:17:45,983
I’ll go ahead now.

347
00:17:46,150 --> 00:17:48,152
Take care. See you around.

348
00:17:51,905 --> 00:17:53,073
See you?

349
00:17:54,074 --> 00:17:54,825
Yeah, why?

350
00:17:54,909 --> 00:17:57,203
I mean, I told him to
visit the cafe again. Why?

351
00:17:57,661 --> 00:17:59,246
Wow, so you two are close now?

352
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,248
He’s nice.

353
00:18:06,378 --> 00:18:08,756
Aren’t you jealous of him?

354
00:18:09,965 --> 00:18:10,883
Huh?

355
00:18:11,634 --> 00:18:12,718
No.

356
00:18:13,844 --> 00:18:16,555
He’s your friend and I
know he’s important to you.

357
00:18:17,014 --> 00:18:19,516
So why would I be jealous?

358
00:18:20,267 --> 00:18:25,230
What if I’m not his friend
and he asks for my number?

359
00:18:27,566 --> 00:18:28,984
You know, it’s like this.

360
00:18:29,276 --> 00:18:32,237
If you’re not comfortable,
then I’ll step in.

361
00:18:32,613 --> 00:18:36,033
But if it’s okay with
you, it’s your decision.

362
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:37,993
Besides, we’re—

363
00:18:38,535 --> 00:18:39,578
We’re not together.

364
00:18:40,204 --> 00:18:41,538
And you’re grown up now.

365
00:18:49,254 --> 00:18:52,424
<i>Where are you? Arkin and I</i>
<i>are heading to your condo.</i>

366
00:18:52,424 --> 00:18:53,550
Can I check that?

367
00:18:53,717 --> 00:18:54,426
Huh?

368
00:18:54,843 --> 00:18:56,470
Can you hand over the phone, please?

369
00:18:57,346 --> 00:18:58,180
Why?

370
00:18:59,399 --> 00:19:00,349
What are you doing?

371
00:19:00,349 --> 00:19:02,976
I just want to see if
you’re cheating on me,

372
00:19:02,976 --> 00:19:05,604
since you’re awfully
close to them like this.

373
00:19:05,604 --> 00:19:06,730
I would never do that to you.

374
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:08,607
- I’m not like that, Miguel.
- I know.

375
00:19:08,607 --> 00:19:09,858
I know, I know.

376
00:19:10,150 --> 00:19:10,943
I trust you.

377
00:19:11,593 --> 00:19:12,510
Okay, I trust you.

378
00:19:12,765 --> 00:19:14,391
But I don’t trust the men around you.

379
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:15,836
In fact, I don’t trust any men.

380
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:17,390
Who knows what they might do to you.

381
00:19:17,950 --> 00:19:21,787
It’s just Sevi and Arkin,
we’ve been friends since we were kids.

382
00:19:21,787 --> 00:19:23,789
We’ve been friends since high school.

383
00:19:24,011 --> 00:19:24,887
I don’t like it.

384
00:19:25,332 --> 00:19:26,917
I don’t like it. No.

385
00:19:27,543 --> 00:19:29,211
You’re gonna stop hanging out with them

386
00:19:29,774 --> 00:19:32,026
and you’re not gonna see them anymore.
You understand?

387
00:19:32,268 --> 00:19:33,686
Don’t talk.

388
00:19:33,842 --> 00:19:35,010
I already told you this before.

389
00:19:35,509 --> 00:19:38,637
Okay? If you’re seen with other guys,
always surrounded by men,

390
00:19:38,662 --> 00:19:40,247
what do you think people will say, huh?

391
00:19:40,272 --> 00:19:43,525
They’ll think you’re a whore,
they’ll think you’re a bitch.

392
00:19:43,550 --> 00:19:44,343
Is that what you want?

393
00:19:44,549 --> 00:19:46,259
Tell me.
Is that what you want?

394
00:19:46,630 --> 00:19:48,549
You want to be seen as a slut?

395
00:19:49,129 --> 00:19:50,797
As a bitch? Easy to get?

396
00:19:50,852 --> 00:19:52,479
No, Kierra.
I can’t have that.

397
00:19:53,402 --> 00:19:54,528
You think about me.

398
00:19:54,553 --> 00:19:55,065
Listen.

399
00:19:55,090 --> 00:19:57,134
Don’t look away. Look at me.

400
00:19:58,477 --> 00:19:59,520
Do you understand?

401
00:20:00,102 --> 00:20:03,105
This is our relationship,
not just your relationship.

402
00:20:03,470 --> 00:20:05,847
You’re representing me, my family.

403
00:20:05,872 --> 00:20:07,874
Think about what people will think.

404
00:20:08,831 --> 00:20:09,624
What do you think?

405
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:10,992
Huh?

406
00:20:11,529 --> 00:20:12,822
You’re gonna be walking around—

407
00:20:13,024 --> 00:20:15,276
with other dicks?
You want that?

408
00:20:15,575 --> 00:20:16,326
You want that?

409
00:20:16,986 --> 00:20:17,945
Speak.

410
00:20:18,297 --> 00:20:19,006
No.

411
00:20:20,345 --> 00:20:21,889
So grab the damn phone

412
00:20:22,973 --> 00:20:25,350
and tell them not to come.

413
00:20:25,893 --> 00:20:29,354
Tell them not to come.
Tell them you already have a boyfriend.

414
00:20:30,314 --> 00:20:32,566
Either you do that or you don’t.

415
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:33,791
I’ll do it.

416
00:20:38,147 --> 00:20:38,898
What about you?

417
00:20:40,157 --> 00:20:41,408
Aren’t you the jealous type?

418
00:20:45,037 --> 00:20:47,122
When I get into a relationship,

419
00:20:49,127 --> 00:20:52,547
I trust my partner completely.

420
00:20:52,878 --> 00:20:56,006
Because they chose me,
and I’ll hold on to that.

421
00:21:00,719 --> 00:21:02,679
Do you remember what I told you before?

422
00:21:03,105 --> 00:21:03,772
What?

423
00:21:05,716 --> 00:21:07,385
That I’m scared to commit.

424
00:21:09,970 --> 00:21:13,683
It’s just that I realized that maybe
I answered that way because—

425
00:21:15,142 --> 00:21:18,062
I really didn’t know what I wanted.

426
00:21:19,454 --> 00:21:20,622
But now

427
00:21:22,256 --> 00:21:23,382
I know what I want.

428
00:21:24,910 --> 00:21:26,787
And I’m no longer scared to commit.

429
00:21:37,422 --> 00:21:38,215
By the way,

430
00:21:38,491 --> 00:21:41,135
thank you for celebrating
your Christmas with us.

431
00:21:42,698 --> 00:21:47,203
You know, I really like the holidays
because they’re so peaceful.

432
00:21:47,891 --> 00:21:50,686
And calming, with nothing to worry about.

433
00:21:53,266 --> 00:21:54,760
I like holidays with you.

434
00:21:57,210 --> 00:22:00,797
Uh-oh, Mommy’s going to
keep inviting you to join us now.

435
00:22:01,133 --> 00:22:02,218
Why not?

436
00:22:02,492 --> 00:22:03,451
I’m in.

437
00:22:04,027 --> 00:22:06,697
Actually, they really did invite you.

438
00:22:07,244 --> 00:22:09,913
Do you want to spend New Year’s with us?

439
00:22:10,340 --> 00:22:11,216
Really?

440
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,451
- Sorry, sorry.
- Uncle, Auntie.

441
00:22:19,937 --> 00:22:23,399
Sweetie, before I forget,
did you tell Shan already?

442
00:22:23,454 --> 00:22:24,121
Yes.

443
00:22:24,146 --> 00:22:27,733
Mommy, Shan doesn’t believe that
you’re inviting him for New Year’s.

444
00:22:28,724 --> 00:22:30,809
Come on, just come, please.

445
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:35,603
If it’s okay with you. I’ve had a
really good time this Christmas, too.

446
00:22:36,148 --> 00:22:38,734
Well, there you go.
Of course. Celebrate with us.

447
00:22:39,957 --> 00:22:40,749
Sure.

448
00:22:41,353 --> 00:22:43,397
Here in Bataan again, or in Manila?

449
00:22:43,762 --> 00:22:48,684
Shan, you’ll enjoy it even more once you
find out where we’re going.

450
00:22:49,786 --> 00:22:50,537
Right, Dad?

451
00:22:50,537 --> 00:22:52,164
- Yeah.
- Where are we going?

452
00:22:52,247 --> 00:22:53,206
New Year’s.

453
00:22:53,206 --> 00:22:55,876
It’s going to be fun.

454
00:22:55,876 --> 00:22:57,210
It’s going to be beautiful.

455
00:23:21,735 --> 00:23:22,861
Here you go.

456
00:23:24,446 --> 00:23:26,365
- Let me see.
- Right.

457
00:23:27,824 --> 00:23:29,368
Nice.

458
00:23:29,660 --> 00:23:30,744
Small. Nice.

459
00:23:30,744 --> 00:23:32,245
Right? Isn’t it?

460
00:23:32,371 --> 00:23:34,289
If you two need anything,
sweetie, we’re right—

461
00:23:34,289 --> 00:23:36,124
- beside your room, okay?
- Okay.

462
00:23:36,124 --> 00:23:37,000
- Okay, mommy.
- All right.

463
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,001
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight.

464
00:23:38,335 --> 00:23:39,252
Daddy, goodnight.

465
00:23:39,711 --> 00:23:40,212
Goodnight.

466
00:23:40,212 --> 00:23:40,796
Thank you.

467
00:23:40,796 --> 00:23:41,546
Goodnight.

468
00:23:41,546 --> 00:23:43,131
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight.

469
00:24:08,331 --> 00:24:09,291
Wow,

470
00:24:10,184 --> 00:24:13,187
I can’t believe we’re
actually in Jeju already.

471
00:24:13,527 --> 00:24:14,570
Honestly,

472
00:24:15,072 --> 00:24:17,867
I’m not really one for celebrating
occasions like this.

473
00:24:18,773 --> 00:24:19,524
Wait.

474
00:24:20,397 --> 00:24:21,607
When’s your birthday?

475
00:24:22,864 --> 00:24:23,990
It was back in November.

476
00:24:24,015 --> 00:24:25,224
- It’s already over.
- What?

477
00:24:25,249 --> 00:24:26,584
Why didn’t you say anything?

478
00:24:28,335 --> 00:24:30,671
I don’t really celebrate birthdays.

479
00:24:31,122 --> 00:24:33,583
I just studied,
at least it was a productive day.

480
00:24:33,688 --> 00:24:37,692
Then my friend Hiro sent a cake.

481
00:24:38,481 --> 00:24:40,400
We should’ve celebrated.

482
00:24:40,663 --> 00:24:44,584
Let’s use this vacation
as your celebration.

483
00:24:46,310 --> 00:24:47,394
It’s fine.

484
00:24:47,983 --> 00:24:49,693
My birthday isn’t special, Ke.

485
00:24:49,718 --> 00:24:51,928
It’s special to me. So, shut up, okay?

486
00:24:53,475 --> 00:24:56,478
Go rest, since we have
a lot to do tomorrow.

487
00:24:57,273 --> 00:24:58,357
Where are we going tomorrow?

488
00:24:58,554 --> 00:24:59,644
Lots of places.

489
00:25:00,169 --> 00:25:01,462
Okay.

490
00:25:13,615 --> 00:25:17,744
Happy New Year!
Is everyone with their partner?

491
00:25:17,893 --> 00:25:19,227
Happy New Year.

492
00:25:20,033 --> 00:25:21,785
Guys, Naomi’s here too.

493
00:25:21,810 --> 00:25:23,103
Naomi, say hi to them.

494
00:25:24,973 --> 00:25:26,891
She’s shy, she doesn’t want to.

495
00:25:27,577 --> 00:25:29,496
Hi, Naomi. I miss you.

496
00:25:29,876 --> 00:25:34,213
So cute. She was a bit
shy at the charity event, too.

497
00:25:34,461 --> 00:25:36,755
Too bad I couldn’t come.

498
00:25:37,245 --> 00:25:40,624
It really is too bad.
I wish I could celebrate with you girls.

499
00:25:40,624 --> 00:25:43,794
We’re here in Jeju,
this is where we’re celebrating.

500
00:25:43,819 --> 00:25:46,155
I’m with that person in the back, see?

501
00:25:46,180 --> 00:25:48,640
He’s been eavesdropping on our
video call this whole time.

502
00:25:48,673 --> 00:25:50,509
Shondei, you’re there, too?

503
00:25:50,509 --> 00:25:53,595
You’re so annoying,
you took my spot in Ke’s family.

504
00:25:53,845 --> 00:25:54,930
Hate you.

505
00:25:55,405 --> 00:25:56,572
Seriously.

506
00:25:57,479 --> 00:26:00,107
Imagine, Luna, I was right there,
but I still heard you.

507
00:26:00,310 --> 00:26:01,770
You’re so loud, huh?

508
00:26:01,770 --> 00:26:04,481
Take care there, okay!
It’s probably cold over there.

509
00:26:04,964 --> 00:26:07,717
It’s okay.
I’ll just hug her, Via. Like this.

510
00:26:09,658 --> 00:26:11,869
Does…
Does Via have a boyfriend?

511
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:14,612
Hey, I heard that.

512
00:26:14,637 --> 00:26:16,305
Oh, it’s not on mute?

513
00:26:17,353 --> 00:26:19,855
Who’s calling? I was cooking.

514
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:21,549
Probably you, Luna, right?

515
00:26:21,574 --> 00:26:23,200
You’re really so annoying.

516
00:26:23,225 --> 00:26:25,978
Oh, really? You’ve got some nerve,
you’re not exactly the quiet type either.

517
00:26:26,044 --> 00:26:28,672
Honestly, you need to change.
You never say anything right.

518
00:26:29,214 --> 00:26:32,801
Happy New Year, Via!
Where’s Arkin? I miss that idiot.

519
00:26:33,069 --> 00:26:36,531
Hey, idiots!
I’m so sick of your face, bro.

520
00:26:36,623 --> 00:26:38,417
Oh my god, you’re there, too.

521
00:26:38,632 --> 00:26:40,092
I was memorizing my script.

522
00:26:40,817 --> 00:26:42,318
Hi, Cy! Hi, Doc.

523
00:26:42,931 --> 00:26:44,182
Do you know me now?

524
00:26:44,207 --> 00:26:47,127
Of course. Refreshing.

525
00:26:48,575 --> 00:26:50,535
I miss you guys.

526
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:53,021
